Gate the GunCon manual calibration on the lightgun-flash shader being
the active video shader.

The calibration logic introduced by 0031 (OSD prompts, target capture,
AUX button masking) was activated by default for every lightgun, because
`cal_state` starts at 0 (= PHASE1) and the OSD is pushed whenever
cal_state == 0. For non-GunCon lightguns (e.g. firmware-driven JVS
guns), configgen does NOT load the lightgun-flash shader — so the user
sees the "SHOOT THE RED TARGET" OSD with no actual targets drawn, and
the gun's AUX buttons stay masked toward the core forever (they can't
shoot the invisible targets to advance to cal_state == 2).

configgen only loads `lightgun-flash.{glslp,slangp}` for GunCon 2 pads.
Use the presence of that shader (detected by looking up the cal_phase
parameter on the currently bound video shader) as the gate: if the
flash shader is not loaded, force cal_state = 2 (DONE) every frame.
That keeps the calibration code path inactive for every other lightgun
without changing the cal_state defaults or touching any other code.

diff --git a/input/lightguns.c b/input/lightguns.c
--- a/input/lightguns.c
+++ b/input/lightguns.c
@@ -289,6 +289,27 @@
    video_driver_state_t *video_st = video_state_get_ptr();
    bool real_pressed              = (res != 0);

+   /* Calibration is GunCon-only: configgen loads the lightgun-flash
+    * shader (which draws the cal targets and exposes the cal_phase
+    * parameter) only for GunCon 2 pads. If that shader isn't the
+    * active one there's nothing to calibrate against — force cal DONE
+    * so no calibration OSD is shown and the gun's AUX buttons are not
+    * masked toward the core. */
+   {
+      video_shader_ctx_t cal_sc;
+      bool flash_shader = false;
+      cal_sc.data = NULL;
+      if (video_shader_driver_get_current_shader(&cal_sc) && cal_sc.data)
+      {
+         unsigned i;
+         for (i = 0; i < cal_sc.data->num_parameters; i++)
+            if (!strcmp(cal_sc.data->parameters[i].id, "cal_phase"))
+            { flash_shader = true; break; }
+      }
+      if (!flash_shader)
+         input_st->lightgun.cal_state[port] = 2;
+   }
+
    /* Force-poll AUX_A and AUX_B from inside the TRIGGER read so the
     * cal validate/retry buttons work even with cores that never
     * poll them (e.g. fbneo Point Blank only reads TRIGGER +

